## Oracle finding

Pinned Java `ProcessQueue.makeMessageToConsumeAgain([message, null])` moves
the valid prefix from its consuming map into the ready map, then propagates
`NullPointerException`. The requeue does not change counters or the dispatch
flag. Rust's `make_message_to_consume_again_items_nullable` requeues the prefix,
removes its in-flight ownership, retains count/size/dispatch state, and returns
a typed null-element error.

The invoked Java facade fixture and Rust comparison check the error, requeued
prefix, counters, and dispatch result of a following insertion. Fixture
SHA-256: `2b1daf803430969e4b7bd57f4bc54e9794b3d107b7cc0a1fd5fb1062764efdb7`.

